 curves in the following picture.\n\n![](images/b7/b73b05cb7f58bcce1d684c7f19c391ecd2033eb4c47c59daf896546956a9d42f.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n![](images/b8/b8b4cae5128667b4a75097540bddc8dbb853744aee65e96204cf630ccb30fc68.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387311 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1da3c3d0-ffca-58b0-9973-21ca78efe966" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/93/9355e5a989137d0d74ee803bf0fb0248fc68e4df4aa1843afede93d1bb506a45.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387313} {:answer/id #uuid "1d6c888d-3419-51b8-8e63-8b6f80586e78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/00/00b722a09fef4428d17fc7ff6a301b3860e798b20c44126b63cd381ad2884398.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387314} {:answer/id #uuid "522cd20b-1e88-577f-9897-b7d808dced3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ce/cecc7f28c20523aac9f153022d64da4233ce995e05df3b3e2886b7fb3b20d089.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387315} {:answer/id #uuid "7370d0a5-e8d6-5b38-af6b-5d647d33fadb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/8e/8e30bba74fad98713f891950fd052d2ddd2cb2dc349bd9bcb7efe3333b7203dd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387316} {:answer/id #uuid "da9ecd53-f00c-59aa-9818-8a0bb184f65d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/14/14c453b9fcf4670a2356b730253dd7f411b989abde303f059ebb5a9d559a4eff.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387317}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "522cd20b-1e88-577f-9897-b7d808dced3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ce/cecc7f28c20523aac9f153022d64da4233ce995e05df3b3e2886b7fb3b20d089.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387315} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c14dfe7-e6c0-5526-b094-6b4a396050e0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387312}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "70739974-680b-512e-bb5a-c7c80411f351" :question/math-academy-id "q-122838" :question/problem "![](images/f7/f7dfad4e44184f68de36d455e99895fce8c879d4b053c06aa5805c423bdb1bfc.png)\n\nThe gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y)$ is shown above. Which of the following could be a contour plot of $f(x,y)?$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient field vectors of a function $f(x,y)$ always lie perpendicular to its level curves.\n\nObserve that the given field vectors are perpendicular to the level curves in the following picture.\n\n![](images/9f/9f22df07aac0933106381dce4571e674d656428bf7a976e16bed6d46898f814f.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n![](images/ce/cecc7f28c20523aac9f153022d64da4233ce995e05df3b3e2886b7fb3b20d089.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186407566 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "758d7c9c-7190-58ba-88ca-6ba4209fb9ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/02/02e2b36b593aef6b8477a6e3a546a7a367cd6c7c8de4642684f418222e0d1c96.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407560} {:answer/id #uuid "b0547ab6-4eb4-5605-bedc-e8c09b74d5ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/8f/8f79cfa6b73725479bd76db48b212a60b04ed91f3355c9d135e8cf176b3a6b8f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407561} {:answer/id #uuid "b6af969e-293e-5aa6-8efd-61f10b87dbac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/42/426f761b56bbba7549a5d76ecc6340461c3bc76627c9664a46ef4c6063ee7039.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407562} {:answer/id #uuid "e719fb82-e005-592a-9a1d-c08ce892673d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/5f/5f4468465de36289d11b86acb35c38e6d2034ca220d6559ec93b5085d7437d5c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407563} {:answer/id #uuid "eeddcc87-ac3b-50d2-be15-6abdd930a045" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/5a/5a05d0be8d775cfa97ae507da2ce7904a11b0f7c8df14d51f2e95f17925f64f7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407564}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eeddcc87-ac3b-50d2-be15-6abdd930a045" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/5a/5a05d0be8d775cfa97ae507da2ce7904a11b0f7c8df14d51f2e95f17925f64f7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407564} :answer-field/id #uuid "4cef7ae1-6ba6-5fd3-82d2-e1546e8de597" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186407565}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8917ffe4-7713-5b06-82b5-c913e5f2e407" :question/math-academy-id "q-122880" :question/problem "Which of the following could be the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y)=6x+2y?$" :question/worked-solution "We start by plotting some level curves of the function:\n\n- Setting $f(x,y)=-1,$ we get $6x+2y=-1,$ which gives the line $y=-3x-\\frac{1}{2}$\n\n- Setting $f(x,y)=0,$ we get $6x+2y=0,$ which gives the line $y=-3x$\n\n- Setting $f(x,y)=2,$ we get $6x+2y=2,$ which gives the line $y=-3x+1$\n\n- $⋯$\n\nContinuing in this way, we get the following contour plot:\n\n![](images/d6/d6c45af410df1ae974062b777b856b3960e72ad13e14d37a48e5a92cebf74cd1.png)\n\n \n\nNote that $f(x,y)$ increases as both $x$ and  $y$ increase. \n\nNow, we recall the following facts:\n\n- The gradient field vectors of a function $f(x,y)$ always lie perpendicular to its level curves.\n\n- Moreover, the vectors point in the direction where $f(x,y)$ increases.\n\nWith this in mind, we can add the vector field to the contour plot, giving the following picture.\n\n![](images/3a/3aa601a2bb31bb8c009f554361a79135daf1d7abd2779eaf1ae8b2431a01eafa.png)\n\nSo, the corresponding gradient field is as follows:\n\n![](images/5a/5a05d0be8d775cfa97ae507da2ce7904a11b0f7c8df14d51f2e95f17925f64f7.png)"}] :knowledge-point/title "Using the Relationship Between the Vector Field of a Function and Its Contour Plot"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179714 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179576 :question/id #uuid "2eaebefb-6b18-5689-a746-0d5dc595991c" :question/math-academy-id "e-9453" :question/problem "Find the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y) = e^{2x-3y}.$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient vector field of a function $f$ is given by $\\nabla f.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({e}^{2x-3y}) \\\\  & =2{e}^{2x-3y} \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({e}^{2x-3y}) \\\\  & =-3{e}^{2x-3y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the gradient vector field of $f(x,y)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =2{e}^{2x-3y}\\,i-3{e}^{2x-3y}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd5c5fd8-409c-5b92-a0f1-4466c76cdbe0" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050143 :topic/math-academy-id 1934 :topic/title "The Gradient Vector"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179964 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b255ed32-00b2-5c02-8fdf-4137e45f1f94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x - y)i + (3y - x - 2)j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177454} {:answer/id #uuid "07aeabaa-1756-5d7c-b175-364dae9da70e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2x - y)i + (6y - x - 4)j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177455} {:answer/id #uuid "0ac9617b-4aa8-5c9d-9329-1e2364c1eed5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x - y)i + (3x - y - 2)j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177456} {:answer/id #uuid "56d77004-8bf3-5e3b-9345-4eb6281965f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2y - x)i + (6y - y - 4)j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177457} {:answer/id #uuid "5732c3e7-79ac-51b8-b415-739696a1c978" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(6y - x - 4)i + (2x - y)j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177458}] :answer-field/id #uuid "ca579634-59cd-5d79-9ef4-86d15c0bb68b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177453}] :question/id #uuid "9fe868ae-14fa-5f36-b879-4b4d02b56eea" :question/math-academy-id "q-122399" :question/problem "Find the gradient vector field of the function $f(x, y) = x^{2} - xy + 3y^{2} - 4y$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179965 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ba475e2-be08-57e4-adec-8abff6266246" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(z-2y)\\,i+\\frac{2x}{2y-z}\\,j+\\frac{x}{z-2y}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253761} {:answer/id #uuid "1b833134-f253-5096-a14a-d79dffc93bf9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(z-2y)\\,i+\\frac{x}{z-2y}\\,j+\\frac{2x}{z-2y}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253903} {:answer/id #uuid "1d588fd7-e3d7-55a7-9d28-9f3428789f98" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(z-2y)\\,i+\\frac{x}{2y-z}\\,j+\\frac{x}{2y-z}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253917} {:answer/id #uuid "69fb1b09-9263-5539-88e5-0d8613d52b75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(z-2y)\\,i+\\frac{2x}{2y-z}\\,j+\\frac{x}{z-2y}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254624} {:answer/id #uuid "6e94b4d4-2cb7-572a-9f0d-7088c7794500" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(z-2y)\\,i+\\frac{2x}{z-2y}\\,j+\\frac{2x}{z-2y}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254651}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0ba475e2-be08-57e4-adec-8abff6266246" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(z-2y)\\,i+\\frac{2x}{2y-z}\\,j+\\frac{x}{z-2y}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253761} :answer-field/id #uuid "421569dd-cfb3-59c7-8de4-b002df6d520d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256046}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "68db203b-e688-5d3a-9ec7-9ce2f2bf5402" :question/math-academy-id "q-122404" :question/problem "Find the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y,z)=x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(z-2y).$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient vector field of a function $f$ is given by $∇f.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(z-2y)) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(z-2y) \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(z-2y)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2x}{z-2y} \\\\ {f}_{z}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡(z-2y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{z-2y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the gradient vector field of $f(x,y,z)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(z-2y)\\,i-\\frac{2x}{z-2y}\\,j+\\frac{x}{z-2y}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256676 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0820aec6-52e0-5e49-a59a-3bbb2eaf3087" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{yz}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}\\,i+\\frac{xz}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}\\,j+\\frac{xy}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253728} {:answer/id #uuid "28546720-1acd-59ba-82be-bb4ffaf85ab2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "yz\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}\\,i+xz\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}\\,j+xy\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254032} {:answer/id #uuid "707b941f-3995-54da-8e24-b82c909648d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}\\,i+\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}\\,j+\\frac{z}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254666} {:answer/id #uuid "86a81cb8-c83d-53e2-85a7-df445fd4a517" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2yz}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}\\,i+\\frac{2xz}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}\\,j+\\frac{2xy}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254861} {:answer/id #uuid "d766fd6b-8bc8-553e-b31b-478e1a2b8eac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}\\,i+2y\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}\\,j+2z\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255575}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "707b941f-3995-54da-8e24-b82c909648d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}\\,i+\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}\\,j+\\frac{z}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254666} :answer-field/id #uuid "96de8d74-918e-533e-ac2c-2823c4173a35" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256199}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ec9f81d0-f152-5c1c-b7c8-fd08eb67e7c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-122596" :question/problem "Find the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y,z)=\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}.$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient vector field of a function $f$ is given by $∇f.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}} \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}} \\\\ {f}_{z}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{z}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the gradient vector field of $f(x,y,z)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}\\,i+\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}\\,j+\\frac{z}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256678 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b6a5e9d-527e-52ec-ba7f-90eb833346f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{4x-1}}\\,i-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2y+1}}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254187} {:answer/id #uuid "4210211b-29fa-55e2-a0b7-52ff66e974ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2x-1}}\\,i+\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{4y+1}}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254233} {:answer/id #uuid "445bfc7e-e291-543e-855e-38c46c84f040" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4x-1}}\\,i-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2y+1}}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254250} {:answer/id #uuid "d1e3b28e-4aac-520e-a4d4-79a1adb3c2a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2x-1}}\\,i+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4y+1}}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255541} {:answer/id #uuid "f337cd0f-4b55-5597-858a-91b7156059ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2x-1}}\\,i-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{4y+1}}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255798}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f337cd0f-4b55-5597-858a-91b7156059ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2x-1}}\\,i-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{4y+1}}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255798} :answer-field/id #uuid "0a0aba96-bf2c-522a-b26d-f17993fb8c81" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255931}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bcca6806-23f0-5850-a949-44a533788116" :question/math-academy-id "q-122607" :question/problem "Find the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y)=\\sqrt{2x-1}-\\sqrt{4y+1}.$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient vector field of a function $f$ is given by $∇f.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\sqrt{2x-1}-\\sqrt{4y+1}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2x-1}} \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\sqrt{2x-1}-\\sqrt{4y+1}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{4y+1}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the gradient vector field of $f(x,y)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2x-1}}\\,i-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{4y+1}}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382978 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83468821-c39c-5688-9232-e0a48bb155ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x+2y}\\,i+\\frac{2}{x+2y}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382980} {:answer/id #uuid "c7b76065-e59a-5ca7-9bfb-b669207ba5b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2x+4y}\\,i+\\frac{1}{2x+4y}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382981} {:answer/id #uuid "e411cee5-3a6c-5dda-a344-184fd78d28cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{2x+4y}\\,i+\\frac{2}{2x+4y}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382982} {:answer/id #uuid "e4cc5482-1799-5098-a009-2ed159b19110" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{x+y}\\,i+\\frac{2}{x+y}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382983} {:answer/id #uuid "62c2233e-e9a0-53da-b0de-07b7e76c7fa2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{2x+y}\\,i+\\frac{1}{2x+y}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382984}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "83468821-c39c-5688-9232-e0a48bb155ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x+2y}\\,i+\\frac{2}{x+2y}\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382980} :answer-field/id #uuid "b5b277d7-41a9-51d5-9221-157f88442b55" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382979}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cdc51975-a7a3-5414-a1fb-3bb1994c28af" :question/math-academy-id "q-122599" :question/problem "Find the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+4y).$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient vector field of a function $f$ is given by $∇f.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+4y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x+2y} \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x+4y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{x+2y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the gradient vector field of $f(x,y)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x+2y}\\,i+\\frac{2}{x+2y}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382985 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9dc65a4b-da4d-5350-953b-f73c08bd26cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(z+2y)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz+2y)\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz+2y)\\,j+(x+2y)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz+2y)\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382987} {:answer/id #uuid "36b97e42-68ff-502f-862c-54abe712f096" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz+2y)\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz+2y)\\,j+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz+2y)\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382988} {:answer/id #uuid "f9f60994-da11-59b0-bb31-edf3cb7c1617" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz+2y)\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz+2y)\\,j+z\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz+2y)\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382989} {:answer/id #uuid "344a1d8c-370f-5d8f-9dd1-49c0513501e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz+2y)\\,i+2y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz+2y)\\,j+z\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz+2y)\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382990} {:answer/id #uuid "bb2fc14b-bb86-5f37-bc2d-be43a95e0d67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xz+2y)\\,i+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xz+2y)\\,j+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xz+2y)\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382991}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "36b97e42-68ff-502f-862c-54abe712f096" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz+2y)\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz+2y)\\,j+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz+2y)\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382988} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3294c69-216b-5d6f-aa53-6f52d4c57c1f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382986}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cde4da3d-ec55-5f32-ac16-c33bd9acfbfc" :question/math-academy-id "q-122600" :question/problem "Find the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xz+2y).$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient vector field of a function $f$ is given by $∇f.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xz+2y)) \\\\  & =z\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz+2y) \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xz+2y)) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz+2y) \\\\ {f}_{z}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xz+2y)) \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz+2y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the gradient vector field of $f(x,y,z)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =z\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz+2y)\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz+2y)\\,j+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xz+2y)\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382992 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1393202f-d724-535d-8136-babf2686d7db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{yz}{xyz+1}\\,i+\\frac{zz}{xyz+1}\\,j+\\frac{xy}{xyz+1}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382994} {:answer/id #uuid "a6f87687-52a9-5e53-b8e0-28200e4a81f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{xyz}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}{z}^{2}+1}\\,i+\\frac{xyz}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}{z}^{2}+1}\\,j+\\frac{xyz}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}{z}^{2}+1}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382995} {:answer/id #uuid "4bb0e8f2-8c32-5a43-9f8c-3b04ae890241" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}{z}^{2}+1}\\,i+\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}{z}^{2}+1}\\,j+\\frac{z}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}{z}^{2}+1}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382996} {:answer/id #uuid "b14f2ad2-72a2-5e49-bfaf-d442c2b9f197" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{yz}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}{z}^{2}+1}\\,i+\\frac{xz}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}{z}^{2}+1}\\,j+\\frac{xy}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}{z}^{2}+1}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382997} {:answer/id #uuid "026ff4bf-c0ad-56d4-bab2-b4e07f1395b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}{z}^{2}+1}\\,i+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}{z}^{2}+1}\\,j+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}{z}^{2}+1}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382998}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b14f2ad2-72a2-5e49-bfaf-d442c2b9f197" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{yz}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}{z}^{2}+1}\\,i+\\frac{xz}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}{z}^{2}+1}\\,j+\\frac{xy}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}{z}^{2}+1}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382997} :answer-field/id #uuid "640d3877-8db5-5d72-a910-f0495ca7df56" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382993}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5c11364f-7b1f-5610-8765-613e6f80f65c" :question/math-academy-id "q-122601" :question/problem "Find the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(xyz).$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient vector field of a function $f$ is given by $∇f.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(xyz)) \\\\  & =\\frac{yz}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}{z}^{2}+1} \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(xyz)) \\\\  & =\\frac{xz}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}{z}^{2}+1} \\\\ {f}_{z}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(xyz)) \\\\  & =\\frac{xy}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}{z}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the gradient vector field of $f(x,y,z)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{yz}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}{z}^{2}+1}\\,i+\\frac{zz}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}{z}^{2}+1}\\,j+\\frac{xy}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}{z}^{2}+1}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382999 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "605c17ba-53c0-5224-8301-c7161947f7df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2xz+{y}^{3})\\,i+(6x{y}^{2}+{z}^{4})\\,j+(x-4y{z}^{3})\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383001} {:answer/id #uuid "100cf2d7-b1cf-56bd-b4c5-b50e52dddf3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(xz+{y}^{3})\\,i+(3{y}^{2}-{z}^{4})\\,j+({x}^{2}-4{z}^{3})\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383002} {:answer/id #uuid "cb18d096-f5eb-5578-ad2c-c68d07d3455d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2xz+{y}^{3})\\,i+(3x{y}^{2}-{z}^{4})\\,j+({x}^{2}-4y{z}^{3})\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383003} {:answer/id #uuid "8aee926a-f13b-525d-8f4f-67de6743fd6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2xz+{y}^{2})\\,i+(6xy-{z}^{4})\\,j+({x}^{2}-8{y}^{3})\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383004} {:answer/id #uuid "5fca2b8f-91e9-5173-9378-858ea3cdc4f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2x+{y}^{2})\\,i+(3xy-{z}^{4})\\,j+({x}^{2}-8y{z}^{2})\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383005}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb18d096-f5eb-5578-ad2c-c68d07d3455d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2xz+{y}^{3})\\,i+(3x{y}^{2}-{z}^{4})\\,j+({x}^{2}-4y{z}^{3})\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383003} :answer-field/id #uuid "732edbd7-fdd5-57cd-93ab-a2bf9f45302a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383000}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d9bc952c-6483-5cda-bd93-71113b0eb352" :question/math-academy-id "q-122617" :question/problem "Find the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y,z)=z{x}^{2}+x{y}^{3}-y{z}^{4}.$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient vector field of a function $f$ is given by $∇f.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(z{x}^{2}+x{y}^{3}-y{z}^{4}) \\\\  & =2xz+{y}^{3} \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(z{x}^{2}+x{y}^{3}-y{z}^{4}) \\\\  & =3x{y}^{2}-{z}^{4} \\\\ {f}_{z}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(z{x}^{2}+x{y}^{3}-y{z}^{4}) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-4y{z}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the gradient vector field of $f(x,y,z)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =(2xz+{y}^{3})\\,i+(3x{y}^{2}-{z}^{4})\\,j+({x}^{2}-4y{z}^{3})\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387256 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fbd8e3fe-9258-5fd4-ac38-46ac64db6bc7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{sec}^{2}⁡(x-2y)\\,i-{sec}^{2}⁡(x-2y)\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387258} {:answer/id #uuid "da8671ca-6c00-5ad9-a9e3-7c2197ed1890" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x{sec}^{2}⁡(x-2y)\\,i-2y{sec}^{2}⁡(x-2y)\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387259} {:answer/id #uuid "e5372737-b3d4-5fdf-b4fd-fc53a2121ec8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sec}⁡(x-2y)\\,i-2\\operatorname{sec}⁡(x-2y)\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387260} {:answer/id #uuid "0bcb5dce-0d72-5149-b95d-b553c17f8c50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{sec}⁡(x-2y)\\,i+\\operatorname{sec}⁡(x-2y)\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387261} {:answer/id #uuid "d4e00fb2-b549-5885-b25c-39af3314dd26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{sec}^{2}⁡(x-2y)\\,i-2{sec}^{2}⁡(x-2y)\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387262}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d4e00fb2-b549-5885-b25c-39af3314dd26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{sec}^{2}⁡(x-2y)\\,i-2{sec}^{2}⁡(x-2y)\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387262} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1c2ee55-5d94-5079-b34c-8536d3fd9a20" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387257}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b9b6323d-ff08-50ce-be1a-fa1f61c66864" :question/math-academy-id "q-122608" :question/problem "Find the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x-2y).$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient vector field of a function $f$ is given by $∇f.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x-2y)) \\\\  & ={sec}^{2}⁡(x-2y) \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x-2y)) \\\\  & =-2{sec}^{2}⁡(x-2y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the gradient vector field of $f(x,y)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & ={sec}^{2}⁡(x-2y)\\,i-2{sec}^{2}⁡(x-2y)\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Gradient Vector Field of a Function"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179719 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179581 :question/id #uuid "d41ebc3c-f998-577e-a50b-a08faadd561f" :question/math-academy-id "e-9474" :question/problem "![](images/f9/f9de4a1c2dfb6b8939b2440930eefb8b7020947bd7b943021214adf4cbfce735.png)\n\n    \n\nWhich of the above diagrams represents the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y) = 2y^2-x^2?$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient vector field of a function $f$ is given by $\\nabla f.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =-2x \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =4y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the gradient vector field of $f(x,y)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =-2x\\,i+4y\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we have to sketch the vector field at the points $(2,1),$ $(-2,1),$ and $(1,-1).$\n\nTo sketch the vector field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the expression for $\\nabla f.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(2,1) & =-2\\cdot 2\\,i+4\\cdot 1\\,j=-4\\,i+4\\,j \\\\ ∇f(-2,1) & =-2\\cdot (-2)\\,i+4\\cdot 1\\,j=4\\,i+4\\,j \\\\ ∇f(1,-1) & =-2\\cdot 1\\,i+4\\cdot (-1)\\,j=-2\\,i-4\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we draw the vectors at their corresponding points and obtain the following diagram:\n\n![](images/b8/b88c62b154cecaace206248b62f72b8aa1f71662c0427adfbbabd5c2b4738a6b.png)"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7a43f82e-6682-56af-994a-b0bdf12b4095" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048917 :topic/math-academy-id 3344 :topic/title "Visualizing Vector Fields"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179966 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a4e4f1e4-9db8-5103-b0e7-6bfa97069629" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/56/565dab4b729e587b63826dc9f39363eaf0e941b39188f745b71a336368ed0b4d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177466} {:answer/id #uuid "f0d9eaab-74ea-5160-8a14-8de7f5af555c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e8/e863d2283ea97745102ab489bd7721ad8987c37f33b246023bb2549053f3ebf7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177467} {:answer/id #uuid "1cdb37f0-b0be-50ac-906c-f6836336a177" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/2a/2abd84e2cd0c55cdec95ccb21c8a75270b97d6b7a3bf8b80137e38ab198c24c6.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177468} {:answer/id #uuid "3667299f-b2ef-5465-9b35-0ad04230adb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/dc/dc36c0bfd1e089dc4e5017b4d8eb3fc342aff35ca6b8ce1943a209915592d83c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177469} {:answer/id #uuid "71859476-7f1d-5d93-8176-0d32012095b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/7d/7d9612ef402244aad3a71fb8f8de587eb4be546ad3c1718885c1bafbb1ae1066.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177470}] :answer-field/id #uuid "5efd63b9-13ac-5b6c-ab07-8031398f0949" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186177465} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f2294730-1a63-56a9-975a-ed773eb5c601" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/7d/7d9612ef402244aad3a71fb8f8de587eb4be546ad3c1718885c1bafbb1ae1066.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387182} {:answer/id #uuid "354411d0-1865-5b34-bf67-4f56be47754e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/dc/dc36c0bfd1e089dc4e5017b4d8eb3fc342aff35ca6b8ce1943a209915592d83c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387183} {:answer/id #uuid "311b14fe-ee07-5a20-a6a5-59a701d67acb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/56/565dab4b729e587b63826dc9f39363eaf0e941b39188f745b71a336368ed0b4d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387184} {:answer/id #uuid "0d3a365b-59f8-5560-9234-ece8c5e30b6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e8/e863d2283ea97745102ab489bd7721ad8987c37f33b246023bb2549053f3ebf7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387185} {:answer/id #uuid "b7e37acb-40d4-5fed-9de7-438853dac171" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/2a/2abd84e2cd0c55cdec95ccb21c8a75270b97d6b7a3bf8b80137e38ab198c24c6.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387186}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "354411d0-1865-5b34-bf67-4f56be47754e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/dc/dc36c0bfd1e089dc4e5017b4d8eb3fc342aff35ca6b8ce1943a209915592d83c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387183} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ac480a4-ae34-526d-b6ff-99c48416aa4c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387181}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b5a8a53e-8c38-522a-bf60-158bb8a0f977" :question/math-academy-id "q-122407" :question/problem "Which of the following diagrams represents the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y)={x}^{2}-y?$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient vector field of a function $f$ is given by $∇f.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}-y) \\\\  & =2x \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}-y) \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the gradient vector field of $f(x,y)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =2x\\,i-j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we have to sketch the vector field at the points $(-2,1),$ $(0,2),$ and $(2,-1).$\n\nTo sketch the vector field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the expression for $∇f.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(-2,1) & =2\\cdot (-2)\\,i-j=-4\\,i-j \\\\ ∇f(0,2) & =2\\cdot (0)\\,i-j=-\\,j \\\\ ∇f(2,-1) & =2\\cdot 2\\,i-j=4\\,i-j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we draw the vectors starting at the corresponding points and obtain the following diagram:\n\n![](images/dc/dc36c0bfd1e089dc4e5017b4d8eb3fc342aff35ca6b8ce1943a209915592d83c.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179973 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ba90d78-1161-52a4-93c0-d995aaaf7e51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/6c/6cf967e8a5d3bc7b2ac021414875f5221ef52790dfbdd6e214cccc7f0e8be2d2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387299} {:answer/id #uuid "bb982230-23d8-541a-a311-793fcd335e70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/4b/4be9586aaa886ccfe092f93c106a5f7233509c798c9a90ecfda0363173dc7afb.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387300} {:answer/id #uuid "6f167c07-25dc-5f9e-956f-2fe0933e7ed6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/95/9593ba00b964194c1d91549fe38a1334a478ffd6b724534c4512a11d19d683aa.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387301} {:answer/id #uuid "640a700e-3b7c-59e8-83e6-b88bdc953d51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f8/f814f8c7e6d879cbe25e5108704e29464d0c39859371ee4fac3bfb3e72f90696.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387302} {:answer/id #uuid "09b9b72e-d802-5315-b38d-ee456018cf2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/26/26a5c0123d93231a800456e9f06f6ba7450861838c87d4d1b3ae77dab4cec6cf.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387303}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09b9b72e-d802-5315-b38d-ee456018cf2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/26/26a5c0123d93231a800456e9f06f6ba7450861838c87d4d1b3ae77dab4cec6cf.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387303} :answer-field/id #uuid "a7fe3fc1-2c7d-5b68-96b7-12857eae01aa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387298}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fe3ebbef-9b0f-50cb-ab18-6df5f7b1d83c" :question/math-academy-id "q-122789" :question/problem "Which of the following diagrams represents the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{{x}^{3}-2{y}^{2}}{4}?$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient vector field of a function $f$ is given by $∇f.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{{x}^{3}-2{y}^{2}}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}{x}^{2} \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{{x}^{3}-2{y}^{2}}{4}) \\\\  & =-y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the gradient vector field of $f(x,y)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}{x}^{2}\\,i-y\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we have to sketch the vector field at the points $(-2,2),$ $(2,-3),$ and $(2,1).$\n\nTo sketch the vector field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the expression for $∇f.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(-2,2) & =\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot (-2)^{2}\\,i-2\\,j=3\\,i-2\\,j \\\\ ∇f(2,-3) & =\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot {2}^{2}\\,i-(-3)\\,j=3\\,i+3\\,j \\\\ ∇f(2,1) & =\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot {2}^{2}\\,i-\\,j=3\\,i-j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we draw the vectors starting at the corresponding points and obtain the following diagram:\n\n![](images/26/26a5c0123d93231a800456e9f06f6ba7450861838c87d4d1b3ae77dab4cec6cf.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256697 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f1e18b0-1117-563b-8441-3490065e61e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d3/d3fc823cfcea400219e553f9e6911a312f0a14c7f39aafb49d1af3463cb3e46b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253939} {:answer/id #uuid "46e3f6a4-7353-56bc-8961-cc92fd971024" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/0e/0ea540eb4a48d1fb1777e2d6397e6d38937e9795c4d810b48c0fda0801d1c9ba.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254269} {:answer/id #uuid "64b24222-51a7-5272-9ca7-2db93a07e9b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ba/ba42a974a78df2c0d228e8f5ae543019841c8a7b47e38f02e139fe2d97b8ecf5.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254572} {:answer/id #uuid "8ad5cb04-3d21-55c7-a532-d1bd2ca52b4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f4/f4f0b2e96fa7ee0f1dca7d57a2815e93d77665c0285fa81f2a8b2c5965a39415.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254895} {:answer/id #uuid "bde88cfd-9cb5-56e6-ba40-080493eb0ad6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/36/369ebf19405768bcca19f4981f0237647836250548b0a33f9b4fdba92d85ddc9.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255365}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bde88cfd-9cb5-56e6-ba40-080493eb0ad6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/36/369ebf19405768bcca19f4981f0237647836250548b0a33f9b4fdba92d85ddc9.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255365} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e297b46-c5d5-5311-943f-eb3962e376bf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255938}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3f30aab0-000a-5430-bdac-144d62e4296d" :question/math-academy-id "q-122693" :question/problem "Which of the following diagrams represents the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient vector field of a function $f$ is given by $∇f.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =x \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the gradient vector field of $f(x,y)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =x\\,i+y\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we have to sketch the vector field at the points $(-1,1),$ $(2,2),$ and $(2,-1).$\n\nTo sketch the vector field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the expression for $∇f.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(-1,1) & =-\\,i+j \\\\ ∇f(2,2) & =2\\,i+2\\,j \\\\ ∇f(2,-1) & =2\\,i+(-1)j=2\\,i-j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we draw the vectors starting at the corresponding points and obtain the following diagram:\n\n![](images/36/369ebf19405768bcca19f4981f0237647836250548b0a33f9b4fdba92d85ddc9.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256701 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f4df781-1911-525f-b679-c4fc003bb1e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/0f/0f45b194df67a060c195d4368050cdad9b8bfefab86b41d5eb63723631543d7b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253805} {:answer/id #uuid "4e60cd36-67ef-5e43-b4e0-2891d7e90e88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/92/92f46798ebeae9017c91ddae24e0f68cef81a1045314950bc4b56af003af0b42.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254344} {:answer/id #uuid "ca078818-e709-5a55-8db7-62d422c4af5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/6c/6c76d43daa86b2c8034e3f12592ee6c18bc533034cb255934ff7eb08b2d53623.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255466} {:answer/id #uuid "f4d5cca5-5d32-550a-85a6-767c2bc17710" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/df/df6472974d246217341c69163c2336190980b5aacaa5b1a5c11cbb7126ddde86.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255815} {:answer/id #uuid "ff3b9331-f12b-5cc1-9824-f87b6a349f2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/76/7618ae208ba53f12fb31988a3e0d0cb40f78ddc4348c5049bb09127039c4d965.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255916}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4e60cd36-67ef-5e43-b4e0-2891d7e90e88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/92/92f46798ebeae9017c91ddae24e0f68cef81a1045314950bc4b56af003af0b42.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254344} :answer-field/id #uuid "7db82da5-3e98-5b0c-942d-8b5d0515f72a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256155}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e2b6964a-0bdc-5f5e-bdc8-f351c47c4755" :question/math-academy-id "q-122699" :question/problem "Which of the following diagrams represents the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y)=2y-x?$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient vector field of a function $f$ is given by $∇f.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2y-x) \\\\  & =-1 \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2y-x) \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the gradient vector field of $f(x,y)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =-i+2\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we have to sketch the vector field at the points $(-2,2),$ $(2,2),$ and $(2,-2).$\n\nTo sketch the vector field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the expression for $∇f.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(-2,2) & =-i+2\\,j \\\\ ∇f(2,2) & =-i+2\\,j \\\\ ∇f(2,-2) & =-i+2\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we draw the vectors starting at the corresponding points and obtain the following diagram:\n\n![](images/92/92f46798ebeae9017c91ddae24e0f68cef81a1045314950bc4b56af003af0b42.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256705 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "39ead94b-aaa3-5df0-8bc4-db320602981c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/1d/1da33de6ab53eee30cb7dbdba61a437fd9e3209437d061d2c546386981962942.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254178} {:answer/id #uuid "5e8a3268-82d7-5922-85eb-904111ce9e5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ab/abdb12ae2b6a67283ae65485e124b2a5264ab63a401e8993829f8b56704af479.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254512} {:answer/id #uuid "5fc84add-7dd1-5a0b-9987-6f006015797c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/5e/5e19f0874cbbfcf99c45951c98b19d941c39451c33887fbdcacdb75faeffdc57.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254527} {:answer/id #uuid "88fda897-7ef2-5696-9746-cc266403903e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/1e/1e9b6c550e79abfd03d4ab0c0c7942b5185d24fd2e72203d1cb87c0895e3a6f4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254886} {:answer/id #uuid "c0c76fbf-13a6-5b8f-be2d-44312d2dbaa9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/82/8270942dbaed9f5177e179104bb479802a39c48afa2a528b138b458c042a1556.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255387}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "39ead94b-aaa3-5df0-8bc4-db320602981c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/1d/1da33de6ab53eee30cb7dbdba61a437fd9e3209437d061d2c546386981962942.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254178} :answer-field/id #uuid "b9de488d-3ab0-5329-8a1a-ee5aeb6ecbc8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256253}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f32efae7-0f28-5e13-b999-daa26821b418" :question/math-academy-id "q-122713" :question/problem "Which of the following diagrams represents the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y)=2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(xy)?$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient vector field of a function $f$ is given by $∇f.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(xy)) \\\\  & =\\frac{2y}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+1} \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(2\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(xy)) \\\\  & =\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the gradient vector field of $f(x,y)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{2y}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+1}\\,i+\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}{y}^{2}+1}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNext, we have to sketch the vector field at the points $(-1,1),$ $(0,-2),$ and $(2,0).$\n\nTo sketch the vector field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the expression for $∇f.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(-1,1) & =\\frac{2\\cdot 1}{(-1)^{2}(1)^{2}+1}\\,i+\\frac{2\\cdot (-1)}{(-1)^{2}(1)^{2}+1}\\,j=i-j \\\\ ∇f(0,-2) & =\\frac{2\\cdot (-2)}{(0)^{2}(-2)^{2}+1}\\,i+\\frac{2\\cdot 0}{(0)^{2}(-2)^{2}+1}\\,j=-4\\,i \\\\ ∇f(2,0) & =\\frac{2\\cdot 0}{(2)^{2}(0)^{2}+1}\\,i+\\frac{2\\cdot 2}{(2)^{2}(0)^{2}+1}\\,j=4\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we draw the vectors starting at the corresponding points and obtain the following diagram:\n\n![](images/1d/1da33de6ab53eee30cb7dbdba61a437fd9e3209437d061d2c546386981962942.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256708 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b07ebbb-ae2a-5805-a7b7-426af5bcb497" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/13/135122e85da455699e45c1e276152b20fee0ac9d18441eb5620b1aa43654c81b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254314} {:answer/id #uuid "8fca9e4f-70ee-50c3-8e6c-d0cd30d777a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/25/2595c11a1b30fee9d76028010d2c7e608250c0d48ce0191d7da2a5412af6a110.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254930} {:answer/id #uuid "cc2f9076-3f65-544d-b6ed-94bd3f9e2b0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e4/e4f9011d4497ac01495c1dcde81d9ba19e9b48f9d78c36ca6259d3a2465983b7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255484} {:answer/id #uuid "dba6b19f-483e-5557-90ff-71eb95e4575c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/3b/3bf6311586ae40bb490414108bbf232f40e1e727da45bbdbe3123e60c17f6268.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255617} {:answer/id #uuid "e36ece5b-4544-54b9-8906-c7cdc5544ad4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/71/716f99a985d8b4909e76f922fc3bf5b3350f9cb7496ae0a0a429421016a19267.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255684}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8fca9e4f-70ee-50c3-8e6c-d0cd30d777a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/25/2595c11a1b30fee9d76028010d2c7e608250c0d48ce0191d7da2a5412af6a110.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254930} :answer-field/id #uuid "fefeda5b-1048-597b-a49a-96c4ffaa9319" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256366}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7de89f2b-b3a4-52f5-bd83-f755a3097808" :question/math-academy-id "q-122738" :question/problem "Which of the following diagrams represents the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{(y-2x)^{2}}{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient vector field of a function $f$ is given by $∇f.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{(y-2x)^{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =-2(y-2x) \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{(y-2x)^{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =y-2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the gradient vector field of $f(x,y)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =-2(y-2x)\\,i+(y-2x)\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we have to sketch the vector field at the points $(1,1),$ $(1,3),$ and $(-2,-3).$\n\nTo sketch the vector field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the expression for $∇f.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(1,1) & =-2\\cdot (1-2\\cdot 1)\\,i+(1-2\\cdot 1)\\,j=2\\,i-j \\\\ ∇f(1,3) & =-2\\cdot (3-2\\cdot 1)\\,i+(3-2\\cdot 1)\\,j=-2\\,i+j \\\\ ∇f(-2,-3) & =-2\\cdot (-3-2\\cdot (-2))\\,i+(-3-2\\cdot (-2))\\,j=-2\\,i+j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we draw the vectors starting at the corresponding points and obtain the following diagram:\n\n![](images/25/2595c11a1b30fee9d76028010d2c7e608250c0d48ce0191d7da2a5412af6a110.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383006 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f8bec6eb-8e0a-5ce5-966f-3cfc2e175f0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/fd/fdcd6cebad2e9aef26daf2987b2890a1b05ceeab5f8e803b631cdb4a6a4598c4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383008} {:answer/id #uuid "eee84ab8-4f31-5f75-abfa-e9d0d3f0fc7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d9/d91a13ce4ee54923d33ab5df7506ce8200d02f53695d85d186e0c9f5dc9345db.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383009} {:answer/id #uuid "8f0f9738-4804-5496-8f1c-2a371d83d08f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/57/57ab7ae667788fe307f67df7078d91ee8c0e82f9703d1c59c439a790af9b2fbb.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383010} {:answer/id #uuid "837b5ab1-a135-59d4-bd04-ec207c823e91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/22/2215b79d50f88933aa2b83eb76251eb97a9f3491ffc86b0c5e0eba3debd80cdd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383011} {:answer/id #uuid "c6be86a5-a237-5718-8d27-339f9839dbc7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/94/94f8ffc9b7e98188d2a0429ada7f936df7816e9a04d42e97d3b57e6ab34cfe41.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383012}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8bec6eb-8e0a-5ce5-966f-3cfc2e175f0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/fd/fdcd6cebad2e9aef26daf2987b2890a1b05ceeab5f8e803b631cdb4a6a4598c4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383008} :answer-field/id #uuid "f519e720-525e-5a35-9830-b680df8d1973" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383007}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1b63c956-bea1-5b1b-a3bb-61d243984ef7" :question/math-academy-id "q-122687" :question/problem "Which of the following diagrams represents the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient vector field of a function $f$ is given by $∇f.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =x \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =-y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the gradient vector field of $f(x,y)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =x\\,i-y\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we have to sketch the vector field at the points $(-2,1),$ $(1,1),$ and $(2,-1).$\n\nTo sketch the vector field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the expression for $∇f.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(-2,1) & =(-2)\\,i-j=-2\\,i-j \\\\ ∇f(1,1) & =i-j \\\\ ∇f(2,-1) & =2\\,i-(-1)\\,j=2i+j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we draw the vectors starting at the corresponding points and obtain the following diagram:\n\n![](images/fd/fdcd6cebad2e9aef26daf2987b2890a1b05ceeab5f8e803b631cdb4a6a4598c4.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383013 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1deaab34-479d-5252-a2e1-4b9b7d0982eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/73/736cd2cf5d297363c4546465ef46476107cab0e5ec12de51d1792df827dc6c16.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383015} {:answer/id #uuid "096acd8c-d44b-588e-a2a6-4c831113ad73" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/1b/1b7d5a942e7a4df8f0b1e71051fa527213d2e43abaf411bc5024c66f90208e92.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383016} {:answer/id #uuid "761f05d0-5903-5c2f-900e-e1fb72b55741" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/8e/8efbe2acdfe8530f68a51bf4217c2d7689c491f3a8a412e6f3777cb12932e0fa.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383017} {:answer/id #uuid "bf0d60eb-ac2d-5679-8076-b7429123e536" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/23/235d03d87913ebe00b51a0643920c9565e8ffcb88ab32c63bf47ce3b39429de0.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383018} {:answer/id #uuid "98acb1ee-bc76-53a3-80b8-02da68d6b4eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/59/59c2db214327f1e078c0ddc5770e91db5e3de021b9e16fbf0ae7a29545a633d1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383019}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98acb1ee-bc76-53a3-80b8-02da68d6b4eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/59/59c2db214327f1e078c0ddc5770e91db5e3de021b9e16fbf0ae7a29545a633d1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383019} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ec7584e-69da-56ab-a5cb-c7e9ee2cc549" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383014}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "412a3f65-3326-5eb4-8063-61b8d30c5ab0" :question/math-academy-id "q-122708" :question/problem "Which of the following diagrams represents the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{{2}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}+{y}^{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient vector field of a function $f$ is given by $∇f.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{{2}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}+{y}^{2}) \\\\  & ={2}^{x} \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\frac{{2}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)}+{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, the gradient vector field of $f(x,y)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & ={2}^{x}\\,i+2y\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we have to sketch the vector field at the points $(-2,1),$ $(0,1),$ and $(2,-1).$\n\nTo sketch the vector field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the expression for $∇f.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(-2,1) & ={2}^{-2}\\,i+2\\cdot (1)\\,j=\\frac{1}{4}\\,i+2\\,j \\\\ ∇f(0,1) & ={2}^{0}\\,i+2\\cdot 1\\,j=i+2\\,j \\\\ ∇f(2,-1) & ={2}^{2}\\,i+2\\cdot (-1)\\,j=4\\,i-2\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we draw the vectors starting at the corresponding points and obtain the following diagram:\n\n![](images/59/59c2db214327f1e078c0ddc5770e91db5e3de021b9e16fbf0ae7a29545a633d1.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387263 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c7d1d36-652e-5181-9302-abbb5df8798b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/14/1461b0737bf83fee8e16c1e5e102c36c2042e46935550ebc08a0d5774a561cd3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387265} {:answer/id #uuid "293009e5-bb46-5343-920e-66801c6cfbce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ac/acb2066428e0660e7d4e106acd5faf60600d6f93de0b6cf4c43ee2b5864e6e51.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387266} {:answer/id #uuid "7be00e9c-596e-5c63-ac00-60deba93c44a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/0d/0d5f1fb1b13459937f7bd3ff0ed8b6da641fcd346dc961d7ec5b98be29e45b1d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387267} {:answer/id #uuid "fa9fdbaf-e58e-56ff-981f-39b0969f23ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/cd/cdebaf3d8c07fe6cb26c4fb2c5b72d2bd60dc968b3345fc1c4a5737d8c6c2b53.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387268} {:answer/id #uuid "e227d23f-1359-5012-8c53-e4feec2f7c4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/8a/8a35641fa57b01a95a0c1d5b3dba8a0072b291a6822ac7b2f5e0473b9037796b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387269}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2c7d1d36-652e-5181-9302-abbb5df8798b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/14/1461b0737bf83fee8e16c1e5e102c36c2042e46935550ebc08a0d5774a561cd3.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387265} :answer-field/id #uuid "07a54f60-4401-5cf2-ba14-b1330ea47fc2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387264}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "40689dc7-e924-59ea-9bdd-9f2acdedd9ce" :question/math-academy-id "q-122619" :question/problem "Which of the following diagrams represents the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y)=x+{y}^{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient vector field of a function $f$ is given by $∇f.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x+{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =1 \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x+{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the gradient vector field of $f(x,y)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\,i+2y\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we have to sketch the vector field at the points $(-4,1),$ $(1,1),$ and $(3,-1).$\n\nTo sketch the vector field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the expression for $∇f.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(-4,1) & =i+2\\cdot 1\\,j=i+2\\,j \\\\ ∇f(1,1) & =i+2\\cdot 1\\,j=i+2\\,j \\\\ ∇f(3,-1) & =i+2\\cdot (-1)\\,j=i-2\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we draw the vectors starting at the corresponding points and obtain the following diagram:\n\n![](images/14/1461b0737bf83fee8e16c1e5e102c36c2042e46935550ebc08a0d5774a561cd3.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387270 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bec373fa-27cc-5734-871a-ec77749ea6a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/0c/0c425b6fcb88f4c958a7c0371a64a815eda5ebf8ed14b0adc06875de1e24003b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387272} {:answer/id #uuid "6120694d-f5d6-5a30-a9b1-04836470b4fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/af/af7fdf48d36f477174867761b90d9349344029980012f1f7907f544efd3893bc.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387273} {:answer/id #uuid "5738a2a6-58f2-5cb8-befa-f76d6d0fb2c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/48/48c57f24904442c74178682db34aaa0113eb84042c78516a4e6f961e73b0f9eb.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387274} {:answer/id #uuid "11eee978-2cbc-57da-8a9a-9ffddf6422c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/02/020c3ec7cd0e5e57bb4c6de8516988187c9038d9e5598b116966b71fa8b917d8.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387275} {:answer/id #uuid "04551b05-601c-557a-a5a2-69cba4463197" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/25/25ed4b4750662433bf4405b5e63ab78396688a985c76e2d34d449c0689830380.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387276}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "11eee978-2cbc-57da-8a9a-9ffddf6422c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/02/020c3ec7cd0e5e57bb4c6de8516988187c9038d9e5598b116966b71fa8b917d8.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387275} :answer-field/id #uuid "c39f6b60-6db1-56ec-93e1-e634b438a208" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387271}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "14b7ceda-a408-53c9-aeb5-05da06c84fba" :question/math-academy-id "q-122732" :question/problem "Which of the following diagrams represents the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y)=x{y}^{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient vector field of a function $f$ is given by $∇f.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x{y}^{2}) \\\\  & ={y}^{2} \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(x{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =2xy\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the gradient vector field of $f(x,y)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & ={y}^{2}\\,i+2xy\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we have to sketch the vector field at the points $(-2,1),$ $(2,1),$ and $(-2,-1).$\n\nTo sketch the vector field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the expression for $∇f.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(-2,1) & ={1}^{2}\\,i+2\\cdot (-2)\\cdot 1\\,j=i-4j \\\\ ∇f(2,1) & ={1}^{2}\\,i+2\\cdot 2\\cdot 1\\,j=i+4\\,j \\\\ ∇f(-2,-1) & =(-1)^{2}\\,i+2\\cdot (-2)\\cdot (-1)\\,j=i+4\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we draw the vectors starting at the corresponding points and obtain the following diagram:\n\n![](images/02/020c3ec7cd0e5e57bb4c6de8516988187c9038d9e5598b116966b71fa8b917d8.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186424190 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0afc3cbd-80cd-5f79-95d1-b02b58d14af7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/ce/ce7690cdb4a4da4841dc7f551b73d379945141964de4f9de00dbe6a39a6e36e8.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424184} {:answer/id #uuid "25ed12c7-2e43-5b16-b2e3-173b3c5367b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/e2/e239433cc1c62333506d14eac022488f2c6786837f17f20e6a1fbba9f25dbf12.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424185} {:answer/id #uuid "99f6e268-33a9-5e9a-a609-e6ee2c4c38d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f6/f6264905bceebe59d764a88f8566dc5eb21237dd28ae5c2052fbd3c766ba6c14.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424186} {:answer/id #uuid "c5dba748-9027-5a4a-bf33-0feb67920158" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/4c/4c5c4b297d1aaaa672628f0621e8ed71fbacedd9f418d7d7068da8cba5847315.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424187} {:answer/id #uuid "cad5833b-0aa5-5948-b9b9-b322bb2fcf7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/96/96851fd456d3b9f0a6af941a255926f35e29bbe778ed05556af3f69145e38ef2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424188}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cad5833b-0aa5-5948-b9b9-b322bb2fcf7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/96/96851fd456d3b9f0a6af941a255926f35e29bbe778ed05556af3f69145e38ef2.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424188} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9f1a53d-9e00-54ab-b914-f5c8b1d4efa0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186424189}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6d9aa2a3-1ea1-5a5e-9577-ca5789b6206d" :question/math-academy-id "q-122737" :question/problem "Which of the following diagrams represents the gradient vector field of the function $f(x,y)=(x-y)^{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "The gradient vector field of a function $f$ is given by $∇f.$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}((x-y)^{2}) \\\\  & =2(x-y) \\\\ {f}_{y}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}((x-y)^{2}) \\\\  & =-2(x-y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the gradient vector field of $f(x,y)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =2(x-y)\\,i-2(x-y)\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we have to sketch the vector field at the points $(2,1),$ $(1,2),$ and $(1,-1).$\n\nTo sketch the vector field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the expression for $∇f.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(2,1) & =2\\cdot (2-1)\\,i-2\\cdot (2-1)\\,j=2\\,i-2\\,j \\\\ ∇f(1,2) & =2\\cdot (1-2)\\,i-2\\cdot (1-2)\\,j=-2\\,i+2\\,j \\\\ ∇f(1,-1) & =2\\cdot (1-(-1))\\,i-2\\cdot (1-(-1))\\,j=4\\,i-4\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we draw the vectors starting at the corresponding points and obtain the following diagram:\n\n![](images/96/96851fd456d3b9f0a6af941a255926f35e29bbe778ed05556af3f69145e38ef2.png)"}] :knowledge-point/title "Sketching the Gradient Vector Field of a Function"}]}
